  "highlights": [
    "One view of what needs attention — Command Center, Services, Observer, and the tray share issue classifications and counts. Service health, discoveries, approvals, and configuration problems appear together, with actionable issues separated from information, deferred work, and choices that need your preference. AI clients with MCP access can inspect the same issues, preview concrete fixes, and follow each step's outcome.",
    "Tell Switchboard when a service should run — choose Run when needed or Expected to stay running in Service Detail or the service editor. Deliberate stops are remembered across app restarts, so an intentionally stopped service is not treated as an outage.",
    "AI clients get clearer starting guidance — assistants receive concise setup guidance and workflows that match their current access. They can find relevant capabilities more easily, request a fresh discovery scan, and see whether the information they receive is current or incomplete."
  ],
